      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town originally sat on the Quilcene River banks before being moved to higher ground to avoid flooding.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quilcene%2C_Washington",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Quilcene hosts one of the world’s largest oyster hatcheries, where the U.S. Fish and Wildlife Service also raises coho salmon for tribal programs.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20,
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
